    "defect": "The planted set is built with Array.filter, which discards contiguity, and slide is then summed between CONSECUTIVE SURVIVING samples. Frames from two different stance phases end up adjacent, so each swing-phase jump between them is added to the slide. A clip with one stance phase is over-counted by exactly zero; MB_Walk_Gun_Debug has six per foot and is over-counted by 53% on Foot.L (naive 3.2981 m against a contiguous 2.1617 m).",
    "secondDefect": "The 3 cm band is a fixed absolute window, so when a clip feet barely lift the band swallows the swing phase and the metric degenerates into total foot path length. MB_Walk_Gun_Debug feet lift 0.0935 m and 60 of its 76 frames land inside the band (79%); authored Walk feet lift 0.196 m and 11 of 33 do (33%). That asymmetry, times the 2.3x clip length, is the whole of the 5.3x ratio an earlier draft of this evidence reported as the deciding number. It was withdrawn.",
